description:
Add rolling/expanding window backtesting support to PostProcessor with horizon-aware calibration for evaluating and applying calibration across multiple train/test splits.

## Proposed API

```rust
let config = BacktestConfig::new()
    .initial_window(100)    // minimum training samples
    .step(10)               // step between folds
    .horizon(7)             // forecast horizon per fold
    .expanding(true)        // expanding vs rolling window
    .horizon_aware(true);   // separate calibration per horizon

let results = processor.backtest(&forecasts, &actuals, config)?;

// Aggregated metrics
results.coverage();              // empirical coverage across all folds
results.calibration_error();     // deviation from nominal coverage
results.interval_widths();       // average interval widths
results.n_folds();               // number of backtest folds

// Per-horizon metrics (when horizon_aware=true)
results.coverage_by_horizon();   // HashMap<usize, f64>
results.widths_by_horizon();     // error typically grows with horizon

// Per-fold access
for fold in results.folds() {
    fold.train_size();
    fold.test_size();
    fold.predictions();
    fold.coverage();
}

// Get calibrated model for production use
let calibrated = results.calibrated_model()?;           // pooled
let calibrated_h = results.calibrated_model_horizon()?; // per-horizon

// Apply to future forecasts
let intervals = processor.predict_intervals(&calibrated, &future)?;

// Or with horizon-aware model
let intervals_by_h = processor.predict_intervals_by_horizon(
    &calibrated_h, 
    &future_forecasts,  // shape: [horizon, n_series] or similar
)?;
```

## Horizon-Aware Calibration

Forecast errors typically grow with horizon. Horizon-aware mode:
- Groups backtest residuals by forecast horizon (h=1, h=2, ..., h=H)
- Trains separate postprocessor per horizon
- Returns `CalibratedModelByHorizon` with per-horizon models
- `predict_intervals_by_horizon()` applies correct model per step

```rust
// Example: 7-day ahead forecasts with horizon-specific intervals
let config = BacktestConfig::new()
    .horizon(7)
    .horizon_aware(true);

let results = processor.backtest(&forecasts, &actuals, config)?;

// h=1 might have ±0.5 intervals, h=7 might have ±2.0 intervals
for h in 1..=7 {
    println!("Horizon {}: coverage={:.2}%, width={:.2}", 
        h,
        results.coverage_by_horizon()[&h] * 100.0,
        results.widths_by_horizon()[&h]
    );
}
```

## Data Format for Multi-Horizon

```rust
// Option A: Flat with horizon labels
struct HorizonForecast {
    value: f64,
    horizon: usize,
    fold: usize,
}

// Option B: Matrix format [n_folds, horizon]
let forecasts: Vec<Vec<f64>> = vec![
    vec![10.0, 10.5, 11.0, ...],  // fold 0: h=1..H
    vec![12.0, 12.3, 12.8, ...],  // fold 1: h=1..H
];
```

## Implementation Notes

- Support both expanding and rolling windows
- Return BacktestResult with fold-level and aggregate metrics
- Integrate with existing PredictionIntervals/QuantileForecasts types
- Consider parallel execution for folds (with `parallel` feature)
- HorizonAwareModel wraps HashMap<usize, TrainedModel>

